# Every COPY in services/*/Dockerfile copies whole source directories
# (packages/schemas, services/<name>) into the build context. Without this,
# each host workspace package's own node_modules/ — full of symlinks
# relative to the HOST's node_modules/.pnpm store — gets copied on top of
# whatever `pnpm install` just resolved inside the image, clobbering it
# with dangling symlinks pointing at versions that don't exist in the
# image. Never let node_modules cross the build-context boundary; let
# each Dockerfile's own `pnpm install` be the only source of truth.
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
.next
**/.next
.turbo
**/.turbo
.git

# Generated artifacts irrelevant to any image build — kept out of the
# build context sent to the Docker daemon.
eval-reports
**/eval-reports
test-results
**/test-results
playwright-report
**/playwright-report
coverage
**/coverage
